[h2]0.9.0[/h2]
[h3]Steel decks on legs[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]New: Steel deck 3×3 and 5×5 on legs[/b], 1, 2, 3 or 4 layers high (Paths → Steel structures). The deck appears that high above the spot you point at, with a steel column under each corner that reaches down to the first support: the ground (also under water), a platform or the roof of a building. Every leg finds its own height, so the deck stays level over slopes, terraces and water.
[*][b]One click places everything:[/b] the preview shows the exact columns that will be built, and builders put up the columns first, then the deck. Legs reach up to 12 layers; longer legs are two stacked columns.
[*]If a leg runs into a building or finds no support, the preview turns red and says why. The tool panel shows the extra cost of the columns for the spot under the cursor.
[*]The separate steel columns and decks are still there for building by hand.
[/list]

[h3]Steel legs on any roof[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Steel columns can now stand on top of almost any building[/b], not just on flat roofs: on pitched, curved and sawtooth roofs and on the tops of machinery, and the column visibly continues down into the roof. The legs of the new decks do this too, so a deck can sit over existing buildings with some legs on the roof and some on the ground.
[*]Paths, platforms and other buildings still need a flat roof. Columns never stand on moving parts, smoke stacks, fish pens or porches.
[*]Buildings with columns on their roof keep working and cannot be deleted while the columns stand.
[/list]
